Token.Comment	'-- Each declaration mixes a decidable `Bool` with a loss value, which is the case the loss\n'
Token.Comment	"-- backend compiles to a `where` rather than to one of the logic's own operations.\n"
Token.Comment	'--\n'
Token.Comment	'-- Unrolling `forall i : Index 2` gives i=0, where the decidable side is False, and i=1, where\n'
Token.Comment	'-- it is True. Each declaration therefore reduces to a statement about `f` alone, which is what\n'
Token.Comment	'-- makes it testable by varying only the network.\n'
Token.Space	'\n'
Token.Comment	'-- i=0 gives `not (False and L)` = True, i=1 gives `not (True and L)` = not L.\n'
